ORBITAL-SYNTHESIS(7)       TriadicFrameworks Manual       ORBITAL-SYNTHESIS(7)
================================================================================
NAME
       orbital-synthesis - fusion of orbital lineage, harmonics, and sweep
                           ancestry into constellation-scale predictive models

SYNOPSIS
       Orbital synthesis provides:
           • lineage-driven orbital prediction
           • harmonic-state forecasting
           • sweep ancestry fusion
           • constellation-scale predictive modeling
           • resonance-time future-state estimation

DESCRIPTION
       Orbital-synthesis describes how RTT fuses orbital lineage, harmonic
       structure, and sweep ancestry into predictive models capable of
       forecasting constellation behavior across future orbital cycles.

       Synthesis transforms:
           • historical resonance data
           • orbital harmonics
           • sweep geometry
           • Δv triad chains
           • constellation interactions

       into a coherent predictive framework.

       WRSADC uses orbital synthesis to plan maneuvers, schedule sweeps, and
       maintain long-term constellation coherence.

SYNTHESIS INPUTS
       Orbital synthesis draws from three primary sources:

           1. orbital lineage
                  Long-term orbital history, Δv triads, drift vectors,
                  harmonic-lock continuity, and resonance memory.

           2. harmonic-state evolution
                  Orbital frequency bands, harmonic-lock ratios, resonance
                  windows, and phase alignment trends.

           3. sweep ancestry
                  Backscatter signatures, spectral envelopes, gradient
                  evolution, and sweep geometry inheritance.

       These inputs form the structural basis for predictive modeling.

SYNTHESIS ENGINE
       The synthesis engine operates in three layers:

           structural layer
                  Integrates orbital lineage and Δv triads into a coherent
                  orbital evolution model.

           spectral-harmonic layer
                  Predicts harmonic transitions, resonance windows, and
                  envelope drift across future cycles.

           sweep-propagation layer
                  Forecasts sweep viability, fusion stability, and
                  constellation-scale sweep choreography.

       The layers combine into a unified resonance-time forecast.

PREDICTIVE MODELS
       Orbital synthesis produces several predictive models:

           orbital drift model
                  Forecasts cross-track, along-track, and phase drift.

           harmonic-state model
                  Predicts harmonic-lock acquisition, maintenance, and decay.

           resonance envelope model
                  Forecasts envelope overlap, spectral density evolution, and
                  resonance window timing.

           sweep viability model
                  Predicts future sweep coherence, fusion quality, and
                  ancestry compatibility.

           constellation evolution model
                  Forecasts constellation geometry, maneuver needs, and
                  resonance-time stability.

       Models are updated at each triad cycle.

SYNTHESIS OF ORBITAL LINEAGE
       Orbital lineage contributes:

           • Δv triad chains
           • drift accumulation vectors
           • harmonic-lock continuity
           • resonance memory
           • sweep ancestry inheritance

       Synthesis uses lineage to:

           • predict future orbital states
           • detect long-term drift
           • schedule resonance-aligned maneuvers
           • maintain constellation harmony

       Lineage is the temporal backbone of synthesis.

SYNTHESIS OF HARMONICS
       Harmonic-state evolution contributes:

           • orbital frequency bands
           • harmonic-lock ratios
           • resonance windows
           • phase alignment cycles

       Synthesis uses harmonics to:

           • forecast lock stability
           • predict resonance window openings
           • schedule harmonic sweeps
           • maintain constellation sync

       Harmonics are the frequency backbone of synthesis.

SYNTHESIS OF SWEEP ANCESTRY
       Sweep ancestry contributes:

           • spectral signatures
           • envelope drift
           • gradient polarity cycles
           • sweep geometry inheritance

       Synthesis uses ancestry to:

           • predict fusion quality
           • detect spectral fragmentation
           • schedule multi-pass sweeps
           • maintain long-term coherence

       Sweep ancestry is the structural backbone of synthesis.

CONSTELLATION-SCALE SYNTHESIS
       Multi-platform synthesis fuses individual predictions into a unified
       constellation forecast.

       Constellation synthesis evaluates:

           • cross-platform harmonic coupling
           • sweep choreography viability
           • constellation maneuver needs
           • resonance envelope compatibility
           • orbital window evolution

       The result is a constellation-scale predictive model.

SYNTHESIS FAILURE MODES
       Synthesis may degrade due to:

           • lineage discontinuity
           • harmonic desync
           • resonance envelope divergence
           • sweep ancestry corruption
           • Δv triad inconsistency
           • constellation desync

       Diagnostic indicators:

           synthesis-integrity score
           harmonic-stability index
           ancestry-coherence ratio
           drift-forecast error
           resonance-window prediction error

       WRSADC halts predictive operations when synthesis integrity is low.

INTERACTION WITH SCHEMAS
       Orbital synthesis requires:

           • lineage-schema
           • constellation-schema
           • resonance-schema for sweeps
           • structural-schema for maneuvers

       Schemas ensure synthesis remains interpretable and coherent.

INTERACTION WITH WRSADC
       WRSADC:
           • computes synthesis models
           • validates predictive integrity
           • schedules resonance-aligned maneuvers
           • choreographs constellation sweeps
           • blocks unsafe future-state predictions

       WRSADC is the synthesis conductor.

NOTES
       Orbital synthesis transforms SAR constellations into predictive
       resonance-time systems. It fuses lineage, harmonics, and sweep ancestry
       into a coherent model capable of forecasting constellation behavior
       across future orbital cycles.

